    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 5: Analysis of Sampling Efficiency. The generation length for LLaDA is set to 256, with",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        324.4197998046875,
        503.9974365234375,
        333.4459228515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampling steps set to 32, 64, 128, and 256 across the figures. This corresponds to decoding 8, 4, 2,",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        335.4483642578125,
        505.2481994628906,
        344.35491943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and 1 token(s) per forward pass, respectively. LLaDA enables a flexible trade-off between generation",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        346.35736083984375,
        503.99786376953125,
        355.263916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quality and sampling speed.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        357.266357421875,
        219.2423553466797,
        366.17291259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To ensure fairness, for each setting, we set the number of sampling steps equal to the generated length,",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        393.31536865234375,
        505.2449951171875,
        402.221923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ensuring that in each sampling step, just one tokens are transferred from the mask to the text. We",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        404.2253723144531,
        503.9974670410156,
